<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Clarkson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1764–1828</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Clarkson was a British naval officer and abolitionist, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-clarkson">Thomas Clarkson</a>. For the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone-company">Sierra Leone Company</a> he organised the voyage of about 1,100 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-loyalists">Black Loyalists</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> in 1792, where they founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a>. He served as the settlement's first governor before returning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-clarkson.jpg" alt="John Clarkson" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Clarkson_Baseball.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
